  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oregon federal contracts totaled $2.1B in FY2026 to date. Award volume reached 10,683 contracts, with an average award size of $198K, and obligations rose up 1.7% year over year. The Department of Defense was the largest buying agency, obligating $1.1B. Ship Building and Repairing was the largest industry by obligations, receiving $598M. Major vendors included VIGOR MARINE LLC with $579M and COLLINS ELBIT VISION SYSTEMS, LLC with $196M. Procurement activity also included significant commitments from the Department of Agriculture at $379M and several construction and transportation industries such as Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $164M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $93.5M. Fiscal-year comparisons show obligations of $1.8B in FY21, $1.9B in FY22, $2.5B in FY23, $2.4B in FY24, $2.1B in FY25, and $2.1B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What agencies are driving Oregon contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B and led buying in Oregon. The Department of Agriculture obligated $379M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $146M. Other significant buyers included the Department of Veterans Affairs at $119M and the Department of Homeland Security at $115M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries received the largest obligations in Oregon?",
        "body": "VIGOR MARINE LLC received $579M, making the company the top vendor by obligations. Ship Building and Repairing led industries with $598M, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $219M. Additional large industry recipients included Support Activities for Forestry at $171M and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $164M."
      }
    ]
  },
